{"id": "EUVD-2026-2225", "enisaUuid": "a54fa686-34bf-3012-9c38-e1c6aee8906e", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nipv4: Fix reference count leak when using error routes with nexthop objects\n\nWhen a nexthop object is deleted, it is marked as dead and then\nfib_table_flush() is called to flush all the routes that are using the\ndead nexthop.\n\nThe current logic in fib_table_flush() is to only flush error routes\n(e.g., blackhole) when it is called as part of network namespace\ndismantle (i.e., with flush_all=true). Therefore, error routes are not\nflushed when their nexthop object is deleted:\n\n # ip link add name dummy1 up type dummy\n # ip nexthop add id 1 dev dummy1\n # ip route add 198.51.100.1/32 nhid 1\n # ip route add blackhole 198.51.100.2/32 nhid 1\n # ip nexthop del id 1\n # ip route show\n blackhole 198.51.100.2 nhid 1 dev dummy1\n\nAs such, they keep holding a reference on the nexthop object which in\nturn holds a reference on the nexthop device, resulting in a reference\ncount leak:\n\n # ip link del dev dummy1\n [   70.516258] unregister_netdevice: waiting for dummy1 to become free. Usage count = 2\n\nFix by flushing error routes when their nexthop is marked as dead.\n\nIPv6 does not suffer from this problem.", "datePublished": "2026-01-13T15:34:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:15:12", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5de7ad7e18356e39e8fbf7edd185a5faaf4f385a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/33ff5c207c873215e54e6176624ed57423cb7dea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/30386e090c49e803c0616a7147e43409c32a2b0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5979338c83012110ccd45cae6517591770bfe536", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee4183501ea556dca31f5ffd8690aa9fd25b609f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e3fc381320d04e4a74311e576a86cac49a16fc43", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac782f4e3bfcde145b8a7f8af31d9422d94d172a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2025-71097", "GHSA-hc39-xg82-jgf4"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0035720c-2041-3bae-9990-134e8de47a39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "493ced1ac47c48bb86d9d4e8e87df8592be85a0e <5de7ad7e18356e39e8fbf7edd185a5faaf4f385a"}, {"id": "0e872a65-48dc-3870-b58b-329756c34720", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "493ced1ac47c48bb86d9d4e8e87df8592be85a0e <5979338c83012110ccd45cae6517591770bfe536"}, {"id": "156a1b6d-c3ef-32b0-8caf-8bed7f8c2db8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.198"}, {"id": "1cd79559-f827-3791-8c57-c8117f6c8b23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "493ced1ac47c48bb86d9d4e8e87df8592be85a0e <ee4183501ea556dca31f5ffd8690aa9fd25b609f"}, {"id": "2149d427-2504-3591-afc2-f34f7a336bac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "493ced1ac47c48bb86d9d4e8e87df8592be85a0e <e3fc381320d04e4a74311e576a86cac49a16fc43"}, {"id": "596b603f-a465-317b-9f86-1d8632847741", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.64"}, {"id": "74b7a4b1-bb5e-340f-9307-d89a0ec065aa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.120"}, {"id": "83b9731b-0bef-344f-b93b-790e7bb66047", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "493ced1ac47c48bb86d9d4e8e87df8592be85a0e <33ff5c207c873215e54e6176624ed57423cb7dea"}, {"id": "8adc83fa-b282-3359-a0d2-b23b6b29ac88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "493ced1ac47c48bb86d9d4e8e87df8592be85a0e <ac782f4e3bfcde145b8a7f8af31d9422d94d172a"}, {"id": "9327bd26-323e-3c42-8129-18302fa285f7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c736e30b-dde2-3388-a1eb-98a2d1a60a5e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.4"}, {"id": "d8fe6f48-659e-3f4d-a1dd-44aadfdd9dd8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "493ced1ac47c48bb86d9d4e8e87df8592be85a0e <30386e090c49e803c0616a7147e43409c32a2b0e"}, {"id": "db5b0d2c-8f54-3c8a-97b2-f7efe5a5e7e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.19"}, {"id": "e115080b-f65f-36bc-a866-ab1a84ccdc8f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.3"}, {"id": "e3ae2dcc-5183-34a7-b4d2-a2d6a13097b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.248"}, {"id": "e59bbe2f-6a0d-3b5e-ac45-161c0336e642", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.160"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "022b3ad2-63a2-3b47-9b1c-ed11e7af2a7a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}